00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:27.000
So, one great thing about Ray
Train is that what it can do is

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.640
if there is a failure
at any point,

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:32.970
it can really easily resume

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:36.390
from where it left
off, even mid-epoch.

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:40.290
So, you're not having as many
failed runs and you're able

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.720
to resume your
runs as well, too.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:46.380
So, it -- it is really able
to work with the scale

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:48.990
where things are
not always running

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:51.270
as seamlessly as we want.

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:54.990
As we do just one machine on
my laptop, this is being able

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:59.970
to scale the thousands of GPUs
and still run in a reliable way.

