keeping the GPU always fed

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:55.140
as in it always has
data to work on.

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:57.420
So, you're fully
utilizing your GPU.

00:14:57.420 --> 00:15:01.410
You're not getting those
20, 30 % GPU utilization,

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:05.520
which is such a shame because we
have such little availability

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:08.700
of GPUs and if you're
not keeping them fed,

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:11.550
you're wasting money or
just wasting the potential

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.380
of how good your model can get.

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:17.490
So, Ray data is streaming
the data always to the GPU,

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:20.070
keeping it ready to go.

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:23.310
And so, that's pretty awesome
